{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Awake.</b> All the commentators agreed that this prophecy still pertains to the future, even though it goes back to mention, \"Depart, go out from there\" (Isaiah 52:11). And this is the answer of R. Moses the Kohen, of blessed memory, and it says nothing at all, as I shall explain. For if we say that this prophecy concerns the exile of Babylon and the return of the exile, behold it is written, \"he shall no more come into you, the uncircumcised and the unclean,\" and it is written, \"for this is to Me like the waters of Noah; as I swore\" (Isaiah 54:9), and behold it is a decree that shall not be annulled at all:" "And <b>come</b> comes after \"no more,\" like \"speak not exceedingly\" (I Samuel 2:3), and the letter shin is missing, and it is a way of elegance in the language:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {0 "Resolved the epithet ר' משה הכהן as 'R. Moses the Kohen' following the standard reference; no further identification added."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:08.338072209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}